    "body": "We could define implicit conversions code point → number and byte → number (whatwg/infra#319) and perhaps the other way around too. But even if we don't, we could use short algorithmic phrases inside the formula: \"0xF780 + (byte's value) &minus; 0x80\".\r\n\r\nThere are other formulas in the standard that use byte or code point values directly, though, and they should be changed accordingly. (Interestingly, there are formulas dealing with code units around TextEncoder and TextEncoderStream, which don't have this problem because code units seem to be defined directly as a number type.)",
